# Testing policy (mandatory, all phases, until the user changes it)

Feature development first. Verify only what changed.

## Scope
- Test only the functionality being developed, modified or fixed.
- Do not run unrelated native tests or GUI checks.
- Never run full regression (`scripts\run-regression.ps1`, or every native test plus every GUI check) without explicit user approval. Do not run it automatically at the end of a phase.
- If broader testing seems necessary, explain why and ask the user before running it.

## Smallest necessary build
- Renderer/Electron-only change: TypeScript check for the touched project (`npx tsc -p tsconfig.json --noEmit` or `tsconfig.electron.json`) and `npm run build` only if the change must run in the app. No native rebuild.
- Native change: `scripts\build-engine.ps1`, then only the native tests that cover the change. Before rebuilding, check for a running Music Studio Pro window; ask the user to close it, never force-close it.
- GUI verification: run only the one relevant check and phase (for example `MSP_AUTO_CHECK` build), not the other GUI checks.

## Reporting
- List exactly which commands and tests were executed, with their results.
- Mark every test that was not executed as NOT RUN. Never claim an unexecuted test passed.
- Microphone tests are always: NOT RUN — NO HARDWARE.

## Preservation
- Preserve all existing tests and functionality; do not delete or weaken tests to make a change pass.
- Do not build installers or release packages.

## Example report
```
Executed:
- npx tsc -p tsconfig.json --noEmit: exit 0
- auto-build GUI check: 16 PASS, 0 FAIL
Not run: full regression, other GUI checks, native tests (no native change)
Microphone: NOT RUN — NO HARDWARE
```
